{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790262332844,"sessionID":"ses_f2c0e458effeis5iBSwTK7Szq4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_6e07ad11804349ca8747108d","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Explore workspace structure","prompt":"Explore the /workspace directory thoroughly. I need to understand:\n1. The full directory structure (all files and folders)\n2. The content of addons/shaderV/uv/distortionUV.gd\n3. The content of any .tscn files that might contain a \"Main\" node\n4. Where shaderV_icon.png is located\n5. Any existing VisualShader or ShaderMaterial usage patterns\n\nReturn all file paths found, and the full contents of distortionUV.gd, any .tscn files with Main nodes, and any other relevant files.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"<task id=\"ses_f2c0df61effeDe1BOjKnrTOg4S\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nHere is a thorough report of all findings.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Full Directory Structure\n\n```\n/workspace/\n├── .godot/\n│   ├── .gdignore\n│   ├── editor/\n│   │   ├── filesystem_cache10\n│   │   ├── main.tscn-folding-3ad5c15c4f3250da0cc7c1af1770d85f.cfg\n│   │   └── project_metadata.cfg\n│   ├── global_script_class_cache.cfg\n│   ├── imported/\n│   │   ├── shaderV_icon.png-5ba8dda3dde1d4196a25cb0adc8c8652.ctex\n│   │   └── shaderV_icon.png-5ba8dda3dde1d4196a25cb0adc8c8652.md5\n│   ├── scene_groups_cache.cfg\n│   └── uid_cache.bin\n├── addons/\n│   └── shaderV/\n│       ├── shaderV_icon.png\n│       ├── shaderV_icon.png.import\n│       └── uv/\n│           ├── distortionUV.gd\n│           ├── distortionUV.gd.uid\n│           ├── distortionUV.gdshaderinc\n│           └── distortionUV.gdshaderinc.uid\n├── project.godot\n├── scenes/\n│   └── main.tscn\n├── scripts/                  (empty directory)\n└── task_config.json\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Full Content of `addons/shaderV/uv/distortionUV.gd`\n\n**Path:** `/workspace/addons/shaderV/uv/distortionUV.gd`\n\n```gd\n@tool\nextends VisualShaderNodeCustom\nclass_name VisualShaderNodeUVdistortion\n\nfunc _init():\n\tset_input_port_default_value(1, 0.0)\n\tset_input_port_default_value(2, 0.0)\n\tset_input_port_default_value(3, 0.0)\n\tset_input_port_default_value(4, 0.0)\n\nfunc _get_name() -> String:\n\treturn \"DistortionUV\"\n\nfunc _get_category() -> String:\n\treturn \"UV\"\n\n#func _get_subcategory():\n#\treturn \"\"\n\nfunc _get_description() -> String:\n\treturn \"Wave-like UV distortion\"\n\nfunc _get_return_icon_type():\n\treturn VisualShaderNode.PORT_TYPE_VECTOR_3D\n\nfunc _get_input_port_count() -> int:\n\treturn 5\n\nfunc _get_input_port_name(port: int):\n\tmatch port:\n\t\t0:\n\t\t\treturn \"uv\"\n\t\t1:\n\t\t\treturn \"waveX\"\n\t\t2:\n\t\t\treturn \"waveY\"\n\t\t3:\n\t\t\treturn \"distortX\"\n\t\t4:\n\t\t\treturn \"distortY\"\n\nfunc _get_input_port_type(port: int):\n\tmatch port:\n\t\t0:\n\t\t\treturn VisualShaderNode.PORT_TYPE_VECTOR_3D\n\t\t1:\n\t\t\treturn VisualShaderNode.PORT_TYPE_SCALAR\n\t\t2:\n\t\t\treturn VisualShaderNode.PORT_TYPE_SCALAR\n\t\t3:\n\t\t\treturn VisualShaderNode.PORT_TYPE_SCALAR\n\t\t4:\n\t\t\treturn VisualShaderNode.PORT_TYPE_SCALAR\n\nfunc _get_output_port_count() -> int:\n\treturn 1\n\nfunc _get_output_port_name(port: int) -> String:\n\treturn \"uv\"\n\nfunc _get_output_port_type(port):\n\treturn VisualShaderNode.PORT_TYPE_VECTOR_3D\n\nfunc _get_global_code(mode):\n\tvar path = self.get_script().get_path().get_base_dir()\n\treturn '#include \"' + path + '/distortionUV.gdshaderinc\"'\n\nfunc _get_code(input_vars, output_vars, mode, type):\n\tvar uv = \"UV\"\n\n\tif input_vars[0]:\n\t\tuv = input_vars[0]\n\n\treturn \"%s.xy = _distortionUV(%s.xy, vec2(%s, %s), vec2(%s, %s));\" % [\n\t\t\toutput_vars[0], uv, input_vars[3], input_vars[4], input_vars[1], input_vars[2]]\n```\n\n**Summary:** This is a custom VisualShader node named \"DistortionUV\" in the \"UV\" category. It:\n- Extends `VisualShaderNodeCustom` with class_name `VisualShaderNodeUVdistortion`\n- Has 5 input ports: `uv` (vec3), `waveX` (scalar), `waveY` (scalar), `distortX` (scalar), `distortY` (scalar)\n- Has 1 output port: `uv` (vec3)\n- Delegates the actual shader logic to `distortionUV.gdshaderinc` via `_get_global_code`, and the generated shader code calls the `_distortionUV()` function\n\n---\n\n## 3. TSCN File with a \"Main\" Node\n\n**Path:** `/workspace/scenes/main.tscn`\n\n```tscn\n[gd_scene load_steps=2 format=3 uid=\"uid://b0x4fw2btt1kp\"]\n\n[ext_resource type=\"Texture2D\" uid=\"uid://c3cqh4a2vmb4j\" path=\"res://addons/shaderV/shaderV_icon.png\" id=\"1\"]\n\n[node name=\"Main\" type=\"Control\"]\n\n[node name=\"DistortionPreview\" type=\"TextureRect\" parent=\".\"]\ntexture = ExtResource(\"1\")\nexpand_mode = 1\nstretch_mode = 6\n```\n\n**Summary:** This is the main scene. It contains:\n- A root `Main` node of type `Control`\n- A child `DistortionPreview` of type `TextureRect` with the `shaderV_icon.png` texture assigned\n\n**Notable absence:** There is currently **no ShaderMaterial or VisualShader** applied to the `DistortionPreview` node. The `task_config.json` instructions (to add a ShaderMaterial with a VisualShader using the DistortionUV node) have not yet been implemented.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Location of `shaderV_icon.png`\n\nThe file is located at two relevant paths:\n\n| Type | Path |\n|---|---|\n| **Source file** | `/workspace/addons/shaderV/shaderV_icon.png` |\n| **Import config** | `/workspace/addons/shaderV/shaderV_icon.png.import` |\n| **Imported (compiled)** | `/workspace/.godot/imported/shaderV_icon.png-5ba8dda3dde1d4196a25cb0adc8c8652.ctex` |\n\nThe `.import` file shows it is imported as a `CompressedTexture2D` using the `texture` importer.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Existing VisualShader / ShaderMaterial Usage Patterns\n\n### In `distortionUV.gd` (the only source of VisualShader patterns):\n- **Line 2:** `extends VisualShaderNodeCustom` -- defines a custom node for Godot's visual shader graph\n- **Line 24, 45-53, 62:** Uses `VisualShaderNode.PORT_TYPE_VECTOR_3D` and `VisualShaderNode.PORT_TYPE_SCALAR` to define port types\n- **Line 65-66:** `_get_global_code(mode)` returns an `#include` directive pointing to the companion `.gdshaderinc` file, which is the standard pattern for including custom GLSL code in a VisualShader node\n- **Line 68-75:** `_get_code()` generates the shader code line that calls `_distortionUV()`, passing the distortion amounts as `vec2` and the wave amounts as `vec2`\n\n### In `distortionUV.gdshaderinc`:\n```glsl\nvec2 _distortionUV(vec2 _distortion_uv, vec2 _distortion_vect, vec2 _distortion_wave_vect) {\n\t_distortion_uv.x += sin(_distortion_uv.y * _distortion_wave_vect.x) * _distortion_vect.x;\n\t_distortion_uv.y += sin(_distortion_uv.x * _distortion_wave_vect.y) * _distortion_vect.y;\n\treturn _distortion_uv;\n}\n```\nThis is the actual GLSL function that performs wave-based UV distortion. It modulates the UV coordinates with sine waves -- the X coordinate is distorted based on Y (with wave vector X controlling frequency, and distort vector X controlling amplitude), and vice versa.\n\n### In `global_script_class_cache.cfg`:\nThe custom node is registered as:\n```\nclass = VisualShaderNodeUVdistortion\nbase  = VisualShaderNodeCustom\npath  = res://addons/shaderV/uv/distortionUV.gd\n```\n\n### In `main.tscn`:\n- **No ShaderMaterial or VisualShader exists yet.** The `DistortionPreview` TextureRect has only a texture assigned (`shaderV_icon.png`) with `expand_mode=1` and `stretch_mode=6`, but no material override or shader.\n\n### In `task_config.json`:\nThe instructions describe the intended usage pattern:\n> \"Add a ShaderMaterial that uses a VisualShader with the DistortionUV custom node ... matching the DistortionUV example constants (wave X 7, wave Y 5, distortion 0.1 on both axes)\"\n\nThis implies the expected approach would be to:\n1. Create a new `ShaderMaterial` resource\n2. Create a new `VisualShader` resource assigned to that material\n3. Add the `DistortionUV` custom node to the VisualShader graph\n4. Wire the node with constants: `waveX=7`, `waveY=5`, `distortX=0.1`, `distortY=0.1`\n5. Connect the output to the fragment shader's albedo UV or color output\n6. Assign the ShaderMaterial to the `DistortionPreview` TextureRect's `material` property\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_f2c0e458effeis5iBSwTK7Szq4","sessionId":"ses_f2c0df61effeDe1BOjKnrTOg4S","model":{"modelID":"deepseek-v4-pro","providerID":"openai"},"truncated":false},"title":"Explore workspace structure","time":{"start":1790262249956,"end":1790262332832}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_ff039183-e990-42b3-92f8-d03bab342986"}},"id":"prt_0d3f209d7001dpbtz6DFtRIrtJ","sessionID":"ses_f2c0e458effeis5iBSwTK7Szq4","messageID":"msg_0d3f1bc0b001PH3w6tycT2l9gh"}}
